{
  "summary": "Fixes request body deserialization for binary and hex POST requests to `/rest/getutxos`. Replaces string serialization into `DataStream` with direct in-place parsing via `SpanReader`, applies `LIMITED_VECTOR` to constrain outpoint allocations during deserialization, rejects trailing bytes and malformed hex, and errors on requests with zero outpoints.",
  "problem": "Binary and hex POST requests to `/rest/getutxos` incorrectly report that valid outpoints do not exist. Streaming the body string into `DataStream` with `operator<<` prepended a `CompactSize` length prefix, causing the parser to read that length byte as the `checkmempool` flag and misalign all subsequent outpoints. In addition, declared vector counts could trigger premature memory allocations, malformed hex and trailing bytes were tolerated, and zero-outpoint bodies were not rejected as empty requests.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit 52034e3cfd: \"Writing the POST body to DataStream with operator<< serializes it as a string and prepends a CompactSize length, which the parser incorrectly reads as request fields.\"",
    "Functional test `test/functional/interface_rest.py` was updated to correct a reversed txid byte order and verify that binary GET and POST requests for identical outpoints return identical responses."
  ],
